.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pvc-fn 1  "pvc-fn " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-fn \- Generate control functions and response files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-fn\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate control functions and response files
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pvc\-fn\-gen1(1)
gen1: piecewise\-linear envelope from explicit `(time, value)` breakpoints (`legacy/cmusic_gen/gen/gen1.c`)
.TP
pvc\-fn\-gen2(1)
gen2: sum of sine and cosine harmonics (`legacy/cmusic_gen/gen/ gen2.c`). Named `\-\-sine`/`\-\-cosine` lists rather than the C\*(Aqs positional\-count argument, which has a real footgun (see `docs/dev/parameter\-inventory.md` §15): passing a count larger than the actual number of coefficients given reads uninitialized memory in the C. That\*(Aqs not representable here
.TP
pvc\-fn\-gen3(1)
gen3: piecewise\-linear envelope at evenly spaced breakpoints, given only their values (`legacy/cmusic_gen/gen/gen3.c`)
.TP
pvc\-fn\-gen4(1)
gen4: like gen1, but each breakpoint carries its own transition shape (`legacy/cmusic_gen/gen/gen4.c`): `alpha = 0` linear, negative exponential, positive logarithmic
.TP
pvc\-fn\-gen5(1)
gen5: sum of arbitrary `(harmonic, amplitude, phase)` partials (`legacy/cmusic_gen/gen/gen5.c`)
.TP
pvc\-fn\-gen6(1)
gen6: uniform noise in `[\-1.0, 1.0)` (`legacy/cmusic_gen/gen/ gen6.c`), using the exact `rand()` sequence the C gets by never seeding one (glibc\*(Aqs default state, as if `srandom(1)` had been called) \- deterministic, not a fresh random table on every run
.TP
pvc\-fn\-plot(1)
Plot a control/data file as a terminal sparkline \- replaces the legacy `showme`/`showmeb`/`showmed`/... family, whose actual job (confirmed by reading them: `reshape \-A1 $1 > /tmp/$USER`, then `gnuplot` on that file) is exactly "convert a binary or ASCII float file to something plottable, then plot it" \- not any of `reshape.c`\*(Aqs ~40 other transformation flags, none of which any script in this repo actually uses. No `gnuplot` dependency needed
.TP
pvc\-fn\-response(1)
Synthesize a `.fr` frequency\-response file from a breakpoint or partial table, rather than analyzing a sound file (`pvc freqresponse` does that instead)
.TP
pvc\-fn\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
